<section aria-labelledby="demo-h">
  <h2 id="demo-h" class="type-h2">Quote</h2>
  <p>On desktop the attribution sits in columns 1 to 3 and the quote in columns 5 to 12. On tablet the attribution sits in columns 1 and 2 and the quote in columns 3 to 8. On mobile they stack. The quote uses the Quote style, which steps from 24/32 on mobile to 28/36 on tablet and 32/40 on desktop. The text below is placeholder copy.</p>
  {% demo "Quote with placeholder text", "block" %}
  <figure class="cs-quote">
    <div class="cs-quote__who">
      <p class="cs-quote__subhead type-subhead">Role or label</p>
      <figcaption class="cs-quote__role type-small">Company type, not a name</figcaption>
    </div>
    <blockquote><p>Quote text goes here. Use a real quote, and attribute it by role and company type unless the person has agreed to be named.</p></blockquote>
  </figure>
  {% enddemo %}
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="tablet-h">
  <h2 id="tablet-h" class="type-h2">Tablet</h2>
  <p>From 768 to 1023px the offset split uses the 8-column grid with 16px gutters. The content is 704px wide, with 32px page padding. The same layout applies to the quote in a case study's Outcome block. The frame below is 768px wide, so it shows the tablet layout on any screen.</p>
  <figure class="preview-frame">
    <div class="preview-frame__scroller" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Quote at tablet width, scrollable">
      <iframe src="/previews/quote/" width="768" height="240" title="Quote at tablet width" loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="preview-frame__caption type-small">The offset split at 768px.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="use-h">
  <h2 id="use-h" class="type-h2">Using the quote</h2>
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Do</h3><ul>
      <li>Use a real quote with a real source.</li>
      <li>Attribute by role and company type when the work is under NDA.</li>
      <li>Use a <code>&lt;figure&gt;</code> with a <code>&lt;blockquote&gt;</code> and a <code>&lt;figcaption&gt;</code>.</li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Don't</h3><ul>
      <li>Name a person who has not agreed to it.</li>
      <li>Write or polish a quote for someone.</li>
    </ul></div>
  </div>
</section>
